      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Handbook Acknowledgment FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a handbook acknowledgment form?\", \"a\": \"A handbook acknowledgment form is the page an employee signs to confirm they received the company handbook. A good employee handbook acknowledgment form names the handbook version, says the employee will read it and ask about anything unclear, and ends with spaces for the printed name, signature, and date.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to create an acknowledgment form?\", \"a\": \"Decide what the employee confirms, write it as two or three plain sentences, and put a signature field under them. Describe that to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, and it builds the form and a database with one record per signature. Each acknowledgment form built this way changes later by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of an employee acknowledgment form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A warehouse can send new hires one screen that reads: I received version 4 of the employee handbook, effective March 1, and I know to ask my supervisor or HR about anything unclear. Below it sits a signature line, with the version already filled in. Forms built on Emergent have no response caps, even in a month with 200 new hires.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields should an acknowledgment form template for new hires include?\", \"a\": \"Seven: the printed name, job title, start date, handbook version, the statement, the signature, and the date signed. Collect payroll details and emergency contacts on an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/employee-information'>employee information form</a> instead. The acknowledgment then stays one screen long, and the signature sits right under the statement it covers.\"}, {\"q\": \"When does a separate policy acknowledgment form make sense?\", \"a\": \"When one policy changes between handbook editions or needs its own signature, such as a new harassment policy or a phone rule on the warehouse floor. That policy acknowledgment form names the single policy and its effective date. The handbook form keeps covering the whole book, version by version.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does an employee handbook acknowledgment form template say?\", \"a\": \"It should say the employee received the handbook, knows whom to ask about it, and understands it may change. Many templates add a line where the employee accepts that the company may revise the handbook at any point, even without advance notice. Have an employment lawyer word any at-will or contract language.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a free acknowledgment form that collects e-signatures?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing, and the apps it builds can capture e-signatures. Describe the statement and the fields, and the employee list behind it can later feed an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/employee-evaluation'>employee evaluation form</a> when review season comes around.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I record a refusal to sign an employee acknowledgment form?\", \"a\": \"Give them a decline option on the form with a box for their question, then ask someone from HR and an impartial witness to sign a short note recording the refusal. Talk through the question first, since the form confirms receipt rather than agreement with each policy. Keep the note in the same record as the version they declined.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should employees sign a new handbook acknowledgment form?\", \"a\": \"After every change that matters. HR guides recommend a fresh form for current staff, not only new hires, each time the handbook changes in a significant way. On Emergent, every round's signatures stay in a database you own, beside the earlier versions.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can employees without a work email sign an acknowledgment form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. They can open the link on their own phone or sign on a shared tablet at the front desk. If that tablet already runs a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/sign-out'>sign out form</a> for equipment or visitors, add the acknowledgment as its own page. Have a supervisor check the unsigned list at the start of each shift.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
